{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"DpopVerifier","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"},{"anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Methods"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"code":"DPoP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"code":"cnf.jkt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","type":"heading","text":"Why this lives in the SDK","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"success.”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guarding an endpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"code":"typ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"dpop+jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","type":"heading","text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"alg: none","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". This enum dispatches on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"embedded key’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"kty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"crv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header says.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/verifyproof(_:request:jtistore:)","abstract":[{"text":"Verify a DPoP proof against this request — all ten §21.7.2 checks.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"verifyProof","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"request","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Request","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO7RequestV","kind